  "facts": [
    "RunSlot owns one UUID episode id. Each in-process run_slot whole-episode retry receives that slot id and a 1-based episode attempt. The live slot trace list resets on each whole-episode attempt, and on_complete is awaited once after the retry helper returns the final episode.",
    "Agent.run generates one UUID trace id before its own retry loop. Its rollout attempts receive the same trace id and 1-based trace attempt. The _EpisodeAgent watcher calls on_discard for an abandoned attempt before on_trace for the replacement; only the returned final trace is appended to the episode's completed trace list.",
    "Whole-episode retry calls run_episode again, builds fresh episode agents, and can call Agent.run anew. That new Agent.run mints a new trace id and resets its trace-attempt counter. Stable episode identity does not imply stable trace identity across whole-episode retries or process restarts.",
    "Episode and Trace add plain integer attempt fields defaulting to 1; UUID defaults and optional episode/trace id injection do not persist an identity allocator or attempts across processes. The agent private _run_once signature now requires trace_id and attempt keyword arguments.",
    "Owned rollout backends receive the logical trace id as name. SubprocessBackend.start replaces fixed root/name directories with tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=name+'-', dir=root), producing a fresh physical workdir per backend start while retaining the logical name. Docker creates its own UUID container name; Prime retains service-returned sandbox ids. Cleanup and service behavior were not run here.",
    "The agent and episode retry helpers retain previous errors on the final object independently of current ok. They do not in these loops merge abandoned attempts' complete trace graphs, rewards, usage or artifact payloads into a spend journal. Current retained trace usage/rewards cannot account for every retry's physical request or runtime cost.",
    "The changed retries.py hunk updates documentation only: framework agent/episode retries are off by default and are separate from SDK per-call model/runtime retries. RetryState counters are process-local. Captured OpenAI client construction uses MAX_RETRIES=0; SDK/harness transport retries can have different ownership. Logical attempt counts do not measure every physical transmission.",
    "The CLI final completion callback records run identity and appends the final episode. The existing trace writer serializes attempt fields and writes artifact paths keyed by trace id, then appends JSONL under an async lock with cancellation shielding. It contains no fsync, dedup/upsert transaction or durable budget/attempt reservation; CLI ensure_fresh rejects nonempty existing traces instead of implementing resume.",
    "The exact diff changes no scoring policy, judge/version binding, admission denominator or durable replay algorithm. Per-trace scoring remains in Rollout.close; environment finalization remains in Env.run_episode; only final retained trace content feeds existing episode summaries. Earlier costs are not refunded or made durably idempotent by stable ids."
  ],
